ranch has two distinct triggers ('No fcntl, or one slot file unusable inside a healthy locks/ dir') but AC8a proves only the fcntl-unavailable trigger; the 'one slot file unusable inside a healthy locks/ dir → ADMIT + marker' path has no covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff2825ed1c751f06c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design 'Degradation is SPLIT' first bullet; AC8a","norm_id":"n889c41a76a2f48de","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A single slot file in a healthy locks/ dir is corrupt/unopenable at runtime; the intended behavior is ADMIT + marker, but no test proves it and the reason string is unverified."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add AC8c mirroring AC8a for the 'one slot file unusable' trigger, asserting ADMIT plus one marker whose reason names the unusable slot.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Strengthen AC8b to assert the refusal raises GateScratchUnavailableError with the gate_scratch_unavailable code, a retryable outcome, and emits NO GATE_CONGESTED / GATE_ADMISSION_DISARMED marker.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC8b: 'with store_root() raising, the gate is REFUSED, not admitted.'","Design: 'REFUSE, with GateScratchUnavailableError ... its own gate_scratch_unavailable code. No marker'"],"finding":"AC8b proves only 'refused, not admitted' for store_root() raising, but the Design attaches specific observable contract to that refusal (GateScratchUnavailableError, its own gate_scratch_unavailable code, retryable outcome, and deliberately NO marker); none of these are asserted by AC8b or any other AC beyond the taxonomy-registration test.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ff4f4176a42a5a0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC8b; Design 'Degradation is SPLIT' second bullet","norm_id":"n30fe08ca4e76460b","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["store_root() raises; the refusal maps to the wrong error code, becomes non-retryable, or emits a stray GATE_CONGESTED marker, and no AC catches it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the slot-acquisition algorithm explicitly in Design → Counter: attempt LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB on each of the N slot files in turn, ADMIT (holding that fd through the run, released in finally) on the first success, and REFUSE with GateCongestedError only after all N attempts fail.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'N slot files in the store's existing locks/ dir, each held for the run under a non-blocking fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB), released in a finally.'","AC1 asserts 'hold limit slots as plan_review' then a verify_completion admission is refused — which only works if admission iterates all N slots and refuses on all-fail.","The remainder of the counting logic (iteration order, first-success-admits, refuse-only-when-every-slot-busy) is not stated anywhere in the Design section."],"finding":"The counter's slot-acquisition/counting algorithm is left implicit: the plan describes 'N slot files each held under a non-blocking flock' but never states how a caller derives an admit/refuse decision from N files — i.e. iterate the slot files, take the first that flocks successfully, and refuse ONLY when all N have failed. This try-each-until-one-succeeds loop is the load-bearing logic that makes N files enforce a bound of N; without it stated, an implementer could plausibly acquire a single fixed slot (bound of 1) or misorder the all-fail check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7894a9d11c25e3c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design → Counter","norm_id":"n0e04a1c1badcc603","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wires admission to a single fixed slot file, yielding an effective bound of 1 regardless of max_concurrent_gates.","Implementer refuses on the first busy slot rather than after all N, refusing while free slots remain."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Design → Counter, add: “Admission opens and attempts a non-blocking flock on each of slot files 0..N-1 in order; the first successful lock is the acquired slot (its fd is held for the run and released in finally). Only when every one of the N attempts fails EWOULDBLOCK is the call refused. A slot file that is unusable for a non-lock reason (open/permission error inside a healthy locks/) is treated per the DISARMED branch, not counted as busy.”","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the leaf's new gate_admission.py / gate_peak_rss seam with the parent epic's explicit recommendation to add the concurrency term to the existing low_disk.py/janitor free-space seam — either adopt that seam or state in Design why the peak_rss seam is chosen instead and how the epic's parallel-mechanism/ratchet concern is satisfied.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4729,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Parent epic comment: 'a fast-fail admission seam already exists (review_bot/low_disk.py plus janitor.py's ensure_min_free_space / SnapshotLowDiskError ...). S6 should add a concurrency term to that existing seam rather than build a parallel mechanism -- which also keeps it clear of the mechanism-delta ratchet.'","Leaf Design: new module 'llm/gate_admission.py', wrapping review_plan/verify_completion at the peak_rss.gate_peak_rss seam with N flock slot files, not the low_disk/janitor free-space seam the epic named.","This is a deviation from a parent SUGGESTION ('should'), not a mandated deliverable — the core shared-cap fast-fail contract is still delivered — hence incomplete_enumeration (coaching), not a floor kind."],"finding":"The parent epic's S6 design comment explicitly recommends adding the concurrency term to the EXISTING low_disk.py / janitor.ensure_min_free_space free-space seam 'rather than build a parallel mechanism -- which also keeps it clear of the mechanism-delta ratchet', but the leaf builds a new llm/gate_admission.py mechanism at the gate_peak_rss sea